sts—housing, utilities, food, transport, debt payments—and set aside money for them first. Then choose realistic limits for flexible spending such as dining out, shopping, and entertainment. A simple starting point is to divide income among needs, wants, and saving, but adjust the proportions to fit your rent, location, and goals rather than treating any rule as mandatory.&#10;&#10;Automate a transfer to savings shortly after payday. Build an emergency fund gradually, aiming first for a small cushion and eventually several months of essential expenses. If you have high-interest debt, make a plan to pay it down while keeping a manageable cash buffer. Save separately for predictable irregular costs—annual fees, travel, gifts, or device replacement—so they do not derail the month.&#10;&#10;Track spending for a few weeks and compare it with your plan. Use broad categories and review them weekly; the goal is awareness, not perfection. At month-end, notice what worked, adjust one or two limits, and carry forward any useful lessons. Keep a little room for enjoyment, and revisit your plan when income, housing, or priorities change. A sustainable budget should help you make deliberate choices, not make every purchase feel like a failure." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.yansuu1.jizhang" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[84,354][996,1579]" xpos="[0,0][0,0]" /></node><node index="1" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.yansuu1.jizhang" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[48,1645][1032,1737]" xpos="[0,0][0,0]"><node index="0" text="✓ 回答已结束 · 本轮未执行记账" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" p